      }},
      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "The effects of icariin, a chief constituent of ﬂavonoids from Epimedium brevicornum Maxim (Berberidaceae), on the levels of HIF-1α, HSP-60 and HSP-70 remain unknown."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To explore the effects of icariin on the levels of HSP-60, HIF-1α and HSP-70 neuron-specific enolase (NSE) and cell viability."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
          "content": "PC12 cells were treated with icariin (10-7, 10-6 or 10-5\u2009mol/L) for 3\u2009h (1\u2009h before oxygen-glucose deprivation (OGD) plus 2\u2009h OGD). HSP-60, HIF-1α, HSP-70 and NSE were measured using enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA). Cell viability was determined by metabolic 3-(4,5-dimethylthiazol-2-yl)-2,5-diphenyltetrazolium bromide (MTT) assay."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "After 2\u2009h OGD, levels of HIF-1α, HSP-60, HSP-70 and NSE were increased significantly (HIF-1α: 33.3\u2009±\u20091.9\u2009ng/L, HSP-60: 199\u2009±\u200916\u2009ng/L, HSP-70: 195\u2009±\u200917\u2009ng/L, NSE: 1487\u2009±\u2009125\u2009ng/L), and cell viability was significantly decreased (0.26\u2009±\u20090.03), while icariin (10-7, 10-6, or 10-5\u2009mol/L) significantly reduced the contents of HIF-1α, HSP-60, HSP-70 and NSE (HIF-1α: 14.1\u2009±\u20091.4, 22.6\u2009±\u20091.8, 15.7\u2009±\u20092.1, HSP-60: 100\u2009±\u200912, 89\u2009±\u20096, 113\u2009±\u200911, HSP-70: 139\u2009±\u20099, 118\u2009±\u20097, 95\u2009±\u20099 and NSE: 1121\u2009±\u200980, 1019\u2009±\u200952, 731\u2009±\u200988), and improved cell viability (0.36\u2009±\u20090.03, 0.38\u2009±\u20090.04, 0.37\u2009±\u20090.03) in OGD-treated PC12 cells."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION AND CONCLUSION",
          "content": "These results indicate that the protective mechanisms of icariin against OGD-induced injury may be related to down-regulating the expression of HIF-1α, HSP-60 and HSP-70."
        }
      ]},
